ector2 a(1, 2);\r\n// True if a == (1, 1)\r\nprint(a == 1);\r\n// a = (5, 5)\r\na = 5;\r\n// resolves to function_that_takes_vector2(Vector2(10, 10))\r\nfunction_that_takes_vector2(10);\r\n```\r\n\r\nAutomatic conversions are confusing and may lead to incorrect code, so I would forbid their use by making constructors explicit like:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\n_FORCE_INLINE_ explicit Vector3(real_t p_value) { ... }\r\n```","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99783#pullrequestreview-2469704292","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99783","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99783#pullrequestreview-2469704292"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99783"}},"submitted_at":"2024-11-29T11:24:56Z","commit_id":"b6590e397cf7d0b7452b5229f75f84017f0f2d8e"}]